## Problem 7 {#problem-7}

*Build a report that for each day output average number of flights considering the current and
the previous two days.*

A 3-day moving average uses the window `ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW` over daily flight counts.
January 1 and 2 have no earlier days in this dataset, so their averages use the 1 or 2 days that exist.

::: {#e9f25f3e .cell execution_count=28}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown execution_count=28}
```sql
WITH daily AS (
    SELECT FlightDate, COUNT(*) AS num_flights
    FROM al_perf
    GROUP BY FlightDate
)
SELECT FlightDate AS flight_date,
       num_flights,
       ROUND(AVG(num_flights) OVER (ORDER BY FlightDate
                                    ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW), 2) AS avg_flights_3day
FROM daily
ORDER BY FlightDate;
```
